rd and three flush cards (7d, 4d, Kd), the board texture is wet and potentially dangerous. The opponent's range is wide but likely weak given the passive play, though they could have a King or a better flush.\n\nReason: Since I am leading the cumulative score and nearing the end of the game, minimizing variance is optimal. My hand has showdown value and draw potential, but betting opens me up to a raise which puts my stack at risk unnecessarily. Checking allows me to control the pot size, see the River card for free if the opponent checks back, or evaluate a bet from the opponent. It is the low-risk play that aligns with preserving my lead.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
